NumAssignedWorkers [SimTalk]
Returns the amount of Workers which the WorkerPool designated by <Path> assigned.
Type
Read-only attribute
Syntax
<Path>.NumAssignedWorkers -> integer
Return Value
The return value has the data type integer.
Example
print MyWorkerPool.NumAssignedWorkers
SimTalk
getAssignedWorkersTable [SimTalk]
getAssignedWorker [SimTalk]
NumAssignedWorkers [SimTalk]
Plant Simulation Help 11-3115
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

NumIdleWorkers [SimTalk]
Returns the number of Workers in the WorkerPool designated by <Path> who are idle, i.e., not working.
Type
Read-only attribute
Syntax
<Path>.NumIdleWorkers -> integer
Watchable
The attribute is watchable.
Return Value
The return value has the data type integer.
Example
waituntil WorkerPool.NumidleWorkers > 0
var worker:object := WorkerPool.getIdleWorker
SimTalk
IsIdle [SimTalk] - Worker
getIdleWorker [SimTalk]
NumIdleWorkers [SimTalk]
11-3116 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

StatAverageTraveledDistance [SimTalk] - WorkerPool
Returns the average distance in meters which the Worker traveled from the WorkerPool designated by
<Path> to the Workplaces attached to the stations and between the stations.
Type
Read-only attribute
Syntax
<Path>.StatAverageTraveledDistance → length
Return Value
The return value has the data type length.
Example
print MyWorkerPool.StatAverageTraveledDistance
